---
import Layout from '../../../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import '../../../../styles/equipment.css';
const base='/equipment/13-14/', catalog='https://documents.thermofisher.com/TFS-Assets/APD/Catalogs/M70002%20APD%20AmeriCat_FINALMIDRES.pdf#page=43', product='https://assets.thermofisher.com/TFS-Assets/APD/product-images/HM%20325%20Microtome.jpg-650.jpg', lab='https://sahmri.org.au/research/facilities-and-services/core-facilities/histology/thermo-scientific-hm325-microtome';
---
<Layout pageTitle="Thermo Scientific HM 325A · documentary exterior" description="Inspect a stationary HM 325A housing and an unrelated 2D drafting comparison." wide={true}>
<article class="equipment hm"><nav class="eq-nav"><a href="/simulations/equipment/13-14/">← Equipment 13-14</a><a href="/simulations/equipment/">Equipment register</a><a href="#hm-evidence">References and verification</a></nav>
<header class="eq-mast"><span class="eq-meta">13-14 · DOCUMENTARY MODEL & DETACHED DRAFTING / FIRST PASS</span><h2>Thermo Scientific HM 325</h2><p>Orbit the fixed HM 325 exterior. On the separate teaching display, compare the same triangle at two locations on a drafting grid. Area and perimeter stay the same even though each point’s coordinates change.</p></header>
<div class="grid"><section><h3>Stationary 902100A exterior</h3><div id="hm-view" aria-label="Orbitable historic HM 325 casing, covered front geometry, and separate teaching screen"></div>
<div class="bar"><button data-hm-view="overall">Reset view</button><button data-hm-view="shell">Exterior detail</button><button data-hm-view="display">Detached display</button><button id="hm-cycle">Switch draft</button></div>
<p id="hm-ready" role="status">Loading metric model…</p><p>Drag to orbit and pinch or scroll to zoom. The teal badge switches drawings on the detached display. It does not affect the instrument.</p></section>
<section><h3>Detached CAD sketch inspection</h3><canvas id="hm-plot" width="630" height="450" aria-label="Triangle with immutable labeled vertices on a metric drafting grid"></canvas>
<div class="fields"><label>Fixed drawing<select id="hm-draft"><option value="draft-a">Draft A · original frame</option><option value="draft-b">Draft B · displaced drawing</option></select></label></div>
<div class="bar"><button class="primary" id="hm-inspect">Inspect lengths and area</button><button id="hm-reset">Reset</button></div><p id="hm-status" aria-live="polite">Select a draft, then inspect the three fixed points.</p><output id="hm-result"></output><div class="bar"><button id="hm-json" disabled>Inspection JSON</button></div></section></div>
<section id="hm-evidence"><h3>Geometry and evidence</h3><p>Registry designation HM325A maps to the Thermo Scientific HM 325 catalog-package order code 902100A, documented in the <a href={catalog}>Americas catalogue, p. 43</a>. The nominal 420 W × 490 D × 280 H mm applies to the compact instrument. <a href={product}>Thermo Scientific product photo</a> and the <a href={lab}>SAHMRI installed photo</a> show opposite three-quarter angles, establishing the pale casing, tray silhouette, right wheel and dark front recess. Local dimensions and radii are visual estimates. The front is deliberately represented only as an opaque fixed cover; no sharp edge, functional holder or movable mechanism is present.</p>
<div class="grid"><figure><img width="660" height="440" src={base+'front.webp'} loading="lazy" alt="Original whole view of the pale Thermo HM 325 exterior with an unrelated display next to it"/><figcaption>Original right-quarter render for comparison with the SAHMRI installation image; the drawing display is fictional and separate.</figcaption></figure><figure><img width="660" height="440" src={base+'detail.webp'} loading="lazy" alt="Original left-quarter render of the stationary shell, dim counter window and opaque front cover"/><figcaption>Original left-quarter render for comparison with the manufacturer's catalog photo. The shell over the front area is intentionally nonfunctional.</figcaption></figure></div>
<div class="scroll"><table><thead><tr><th>Item</th><th>Independent reference</th><th>Actual / interpretation</th></tr></thead><tbody>
<tr><td>Instrument envelope</td><td>420 W × 490 D × 280 H mm</td><td>Metric GLB within 0.01 mm export tolerance; specification is nominal, not a precision measurement.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Detached right triangle</td><td>60/80/100 mm: area 2,400 mm²; perimeter 240 mm</td><td>Independent point-to-point and shoelace result on either fixed draft.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Draft B offset</td><td>(−32, +26) mm</td><td>Identical displacement for labeled P, Q and R. Coordinates are read-only and exported unchanged.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Original equipment acceptance</td><td>Serial geometry from a prepared block</td><td>Not implemented or run. No operation, preparations, specimens or manufacturing workflow.</td></tr></tbody></table></div>
<p>The detached draft calculates each edge with the Euclidean distance and polygon area with the shoelace sum. X is right and Y is up; both diagrams use millimeters at the same scale. The instrument, drafting graph and readouts are independent. The report records the authored source version, raw vertices, stable point IDs and calculated metrics. It does not describe an instrument output.</p>
<p><a href={base+'hm325a-static.glb'} download>Metric GLB</a> · <a href={base+'model.py'} download>Editable Blender generator</a> · <a href={base+'diagram-example.json'}>Output schema example</a> · <a href={base+'verification.json'}>Verification</a> · <a href={base+'xr-manifest.json'}>VR action contract</a>. No headset or live hardware was tested.</p></section>
</article></Layout>
<script>import '../../../../lib/equipment/13-14/browser.mjs';</script>
<style>
.hm{max-width:76rem}.hm .grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr));gap:1.1rem}.hm section{border-top:1px solid var(--border);padding:.8rem 0;margin:.8rem 0;min-width:0}.hm .bar{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:.44rem;margin:.55rem 0}.hm .fields{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr));gap:.48rem}.hm label{display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:.2rem;font-size:.92rem}.hm input,.hm select,.hm button{font:inherit;color:var(--text);background:var(--panel);border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:.14rem;max-width:100%;min-width:0;min-height:2.4em;padding:.32em .52em}.hm button{cursor:pointer}.hm button:disabled{opacity:.52;cursor:default}.hm .primary{color:white;background:#245350}.hm #hm-view{height:clamp(270px,31vw,435px);background:#d9dddf;touch-action:none}.hm #hm-view :global(canvas){width:100%;height:100%;display:block}.hm #hm-plot,.hm img{width:100%;height:auto}.hm #hm-result{display:block;white-space:pre-line;margin:.45rem 0;font:1rem monospace}.hm #hm-status.error{color:#a54a34}.hm .scroll{overflow:auto}.hm table{border-collapse:collapse;font-size:.89rem}.hm td,.hm th{border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);text-align:left;padding:.45rem}.hm figure{margin:.8rem 0}@media(max-width:800px){.hm .grid{grid-template-columns:1fr}}
</style>
